TDD RED evidence for T-002's PowerShell twin
(tests/component-path-diff-basis.tests.ps1), captured post-hoc during
quality-gate remediation, mirroring
verification/T-002/component-path-diff-basis.RED.log's bash-side capture.
See that file for the full methodology note (each of the 5 named
fail-closed axes isolated in its own mutate-run-revert cycle against
resolve-component-paths.ps1, `git diff --stat` confirmed empty before and
after every individual revert).

resolve-component-paths.ps1 is a full, independent parallel implementation
of resolve-component-paths.py (not a wrapper that shells out to Python,
INV-008 convention) -- these are genuine runs of the real PowerShell CLI
subprocess, not a hand-edited transcript or a re-run of the bash-side log
under a different label.

Two axes (2 and 4) surface a genuine, pre-existing GAP in this suite's own
design, distinct from the product regression each axis targets: TEST-021.2
and TEST-025.2 do not call the real product functions (ConvertTo-PathStrict,
Get-ChangedPaths) at all -- both are documented in the suite's own comments
as standalone reproductions, for platform/practicality reasons unrelated to
this remediation. Consequently no mutation to the real product code can
make either assertion fail via the registered suite. This is reported
honestly below rather than glossed over; redesigning those two assertions
to exercise the real functions is a separate concern from what this
remediation was scoped to fix (verify and remediate the two named
quality-gate findings), so it is not attempted here.

================================================================================
