Same honest cascading-diagnostic shape as the bash twin's axis 1: the
bogus rev resolves to an empty string instead of raising, which then trips
the sibling "no merge-base" fail-closed check with the wrong message.
TEST-019.2 correctly identifies this as a regression (its `-match
"unresolvable rev"` check does not match).

Reverted after this run; confirmed via `git diff --stat` (empty).

